WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:06.440
"Using Prebiotics to Boost GLP-1"

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:10.244
Plant-predominant diets may play
a "major role in reversing

00:00:10.244 --> 00:00:12.713
the obesity
and chronic disease epidemics,"

00:00:12.713 --> 00:00:14.648
just as plant-based
dietary interventions

00:00:14.648 --> 00:00:16.884
may arrest or even reverse
type 2 diabetes

00:00:16.884 --> 00:00:19.920
and cardiovascular disease
on an individual basis.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.221
In a previous video,

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:23.490
I showed how a tofu burger
boosted levels

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.859
of the appetite-suppressing
hormone GLP-1

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:27.027
higher than a meat burger

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:29.096
in both people with diabetes
and without,

00:00:29.096 --> 00:00:30.831
even though the two burgers
were matched

00:00:30.831 --> 00:00:32.666
for calories
and macronutrients.

00:00:32.666 --> 00:00:35.269
One thing may have given
the plant-based meal an edge,

00:00:35.269 --> 00:00:39.540
though, at least over time:
increased fiber.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.943
The bacterial fermentation
of dietary fibers in the colon

00:00:42.943 --> 00:00:47.814
produces short-chain fatty acids
called acetate, propionate,

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:52.119
and butyrate, which, in turn,
stimulate release of GLP-1.

00:00:52.119 --> 00:00:55.022
In this way, prebiotics,
like dietary fiber,

00:00:55.022 --> 00:00:56.523
represent
an alternative strategy

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:59.059
for boosting production
of GLP-1.

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:02.095
In contrast, a bacterial
breakdown product of tryptophan,

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.797
which is concentrated
in animal protein,

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:05.632
has been found
to have opposite effects

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.868
on GLP-1 release.

00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:11.271
How do we know fiber-derived
short-chain fatty acids

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:13.073
boost GLP-1 in the first place?

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:16.243
Well, all three circulating
short-chain fatty acids

00:01:16.243 --> 00:01:18.879
were associated with
higher GLP-1 concentrations

00:01:18.879 --> 00:01:20.013
in the blood,

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:22.215
but that doesn’t prove
cause-and-effect.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:26.653
For that, you need to stick
tubes in people’s butts.

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:28.855
Getting a rectal infusion
of acetate

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:31.658
indeed causes GLP-1 levels
to go up.

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:33.961
And the amount of acetate
concentrations in the blood

00:01:33.961 --> 00:01:37.998
reached after rectal infusion
were within an achievable range,

00:01:37.998 --> 00:01:39.166
in the ballpark
of what you’d get

00:01:39.166 --> 00:01:42.102
eating 15 or more grams
of fiber a day,

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:45.505
here in the form
of oat bran cereal and muffins.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.641
There’s a third way
to get appetite-suppressing

00:01:47.641 --> 00:01:50.010
short-chain fatty acids
in our bloodstream

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:53.013
besides the top-down approach
of eating healthy food

00:01:53.013 --> 00:01:54.381
and the bottoms-up approach

00:01:54.381 --> 00:01:57.784
of getting them squirted
in your tush.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:00.320
When you consume vinegar,

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:04.391
its acetic acid is rapidly
neutralized into acetate.

00:02:04.391 --> 00:02:06.360
Here’s the spike in acetate
in your bloodstream

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.795
that you get from consuming
about a tablespoon of vinegar

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:09.730
mixed in water.

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:12.065
No wonder vinegar
has evidently been used

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:15.235
to treat obesity for centuries.

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:18.071
Does this all translate
into reducing cravings,

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:20.173
eating less,
and losing weight?

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:23.276
Let’s scan people’s brains
and find out.

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:25.045
Researchers delivered
propionate,

00:02:25.045 --> 00:02:26.646
a fiber-derived,
short-chain fatty acid,

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:29.182
into the colons
of study participants

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:33.820
while showing them images of
pizza, cakes, and chocolates,

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:36.056
and found that increasing
colonic propionate

00:02:36.056 --> 00:02:37.758
seemed to reduce
brain activation

00:02:37.758 --> 00:02:39.960
in the reward centers
of the brain.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:42.529
This was accompanied by
a decrease in subjective appeal

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:45.365
of these kinds of foods,
they didn’t look as tasty,

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:48.168
and this translated
into reduced caloric intake

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:50.103
at a buffet meal.

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.938
Note that this effect
didn’t seem to correlate

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:53.440
with GLP-1 changes, though;

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:55.609
so, it’s possible
that short-chain fatty acids

00:02:55.609 --> 00:02:58.478
produced in the colon
are accessing the brain directly

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:01.014
and reducing appetite
some other way.

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:03.283
Regardless,
does the boost in GLP-1

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:05.185
and the short-term reduction
of caloric intake

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:08.088
from the direct delivery
of propionate to the colon

00:03:08.088 --> 00:03:10.057
translate into
better weight control

00:03:10.057 --> 00:03:11.625
in overweight adults?

00:03:11.625 --> 00:03:15.195
Yes, long-term colonic
propionate delivery

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:18.632
prevents body weight gain,
particularly deep abdominal fat,

00:03:18.632 --> 00:03:19.933
and may even reduce liver fat

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:21.802
in those with
fatty liver disease.

00:03:21.802 --> 00:03:25.305
So, you’d expect prebiotic
trials to show the same,

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:27.340
and sometimes they worked,

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:30.043
boosting GLP-1
and driving down hunger,

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:33.080
but overall, human interventions
with prebiotics

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:34.981
have shown mixed results.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:37.417
And that’s putting it lightly.

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:41.021
Effects on GLP-1 appear
to be highly contradictory,

00:03:41.021 --> 00:03:44.991
with different isolated dietary
fibers bumping GLP-1 up,

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:48.462
some dropping it down,
and others having no effect.

00:03:48.462 --> 00:03:51.331
In some cases, it’s possible
that macronutrients

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:53.233
that would otherwise
stimulate GLP-1

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.669
might get caught up
in viscous, fibrous masses

00:03:55.669 --> 00:03:57.304
and result in lower levels.

00:03:57.304 --> 00:04:00.340
Regardless, results for
short-term prebiotic trials

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:03.009
are said to be
"completely inconclusive"

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:04.878
for GLP-1.

00:04:04.878 --> 00:04:06.980
One problem may be the dose.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:07.981
For example, in this study,

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:10.117
researchers tested
refined-grain bread

00:04:10.117 --> 00:04:11.718
versus whole-grain bread,

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:13.854
and although the whole-grain
bread improved satiety,

00:04:13.854 --> 00:04:16.256
it had no effect on GLP-1.

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:19.659
The difference in fiber content
was only about five grams,

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:21.995
though, which may not be enough.

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:23.797
In this study,
study participants

00:04:23.797 --> 00:04:25.866
were randomized
to get either 5 or 10 grams

00:04:25.866 --> 00:04:28.135
of a fiber supplement
called Fibersol,

00:04:28.135 --> 00:04:31.138
and the five-gram dose appeared
to have no greater effect

00:04:31.138 --> 00:04:32.672
on GLP-1 than placebo.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:36.376
Only the 10-gram dose worked,
which is about two tablespoons.

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:39.045
Similarly, there were
significant delays in hunger

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:42.716
and increased satiety
after 10 grams, but not five.

00:04:42.716 --> 00:04:45.852
And studies like this
may only last a few hours.

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:48.388
The more fiber-rich foods
you eat,

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:51.992
the more you foster the growth
of more fiber-feeders,

00:04:51.992 --> 00:04:56.163
which means even more
GLP-1 secretion over time.

00:04:56.163 --> 00:04:59.065
Eating more fiber-rich foods
may eventually even promote

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:01.401
the emergence of more
GLP-1 secreting cells

00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:03.203
in our intestinal lining.

00:05:03.203 --> 00:05:04.437
Check out this study.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:06.573
Adaptation
of colonic fermentation

00:05:06.573 --> 00:05:09.042
and GLP-1 secretion with
increased wheat fiber intake

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:13.513
for not a few hours
but an entire year.

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:16.116
People who eat whole grains
tend to get less diabetes,

00:05:16.116 --> 00:05:18.585
but even if you switch to
whole wheat for weeks or months,

00:05:18.585 --> 00:05:20.153
there doesn’t seem
to be much improvement

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:22.055
in blood sugar control.

00:05:22.055 --> 00:05:24.157
It turns out
it may take longer than that

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:28.028
for our colon to adapt
to the increased fiber intake.

00:05:28.028 --> 00:05:31.264
Colonic adaptation
to increased wheat fiber intake

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:34.201
takes many months
but eventually results

00:05:34.201 --> 00:05:36.536
in increased
short fatty acid production

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:38.271
and GLP-1 secretion.

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:40.273
This was found
when people were randomized

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:43.743
to a year of either All Bran
or Rice Krispies cereal

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:44.744
for breakfast.

00:05:44.744 --> 00:05:47.013
And there was
a significant increase

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:48.515
in short-chain
fatty acid production

00:05:48.515 --> 00:05:51.184
and GLP-1 secretion
in the higher-fiber group,

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:55.889
but it took 9 to 12 months
for these benefits to develop.

00:05:55.889 --> 00:05:58.191
And finally,
people may not understand

00:05:58.191 --> 00:06:00.093
the complexity of dietary fiber,

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:02.262
thinking that
it’s a single nutrient,

00:06:02.262 --> 00:06:04.898
but there are literally
thousands of types of fiber

00:06:04.898 --> 00:06:05.999
in plant foods,

00:06:05.999 --> 00:06:08.235
and each one may support
different communities

00:06:08.235 --> 00:06:10.170
of bacteria in our gut.

00:06:10.170 --> 00:06:12.439
That’s the reasoning
behind recommendations

00:06:12.439 --> 00:06:15.408
that people take
a "50-food challenge,"

00:06:15.408 --> 00:06:18.078
eating at least 50
different plant foods a week

00:06:18.078 --> 00:06:20.847
to achieve a diet
diverse enough

00:06:20.847 --> 00:06:23.617
to feed a vast spectrum
of bacteria.

00:06:23.617 --> 00:06:25.218
Those who get more fiber
in their diet

00:06:25.218 --> 00:06:28.588
are significantly less likely
to get heart disease,

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:30.090
and die from heart disease.

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.292
Less likely to get
cardiovascular disease

00:06:32.292 --> 00:06:34.794
in general, and less likely
to die from it.

00:06:34.794 --> 00:06:36.196
Less likely to have a stroke,

00:06:36.196 --> 00:06:39.065
less likely to get diabetes
and colorectal cancer,

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:41.768
less likely to die
from cancer across the board,

00:06:41.768 --> 00:06:44.638
and less likely to die
from all causes put together.

00:06:44.638 --> 00:06:49.476
But all of this
is for fiber from food.

00:06:49.476 --> 00:06:51.845
In terms of fiber intake
for optimal health,

00:06:51.845 --> 00:06:54.014
the first line of defense
for disease prevention

00:06:54.014 --> 00:06:58.118
is to focus on fiber from foods
rather than supplements.

00:06:58.118 --> 00:06:59.152
For the treatment of disease,

00:06:59.152 --> 00:07:01.221
there is a lack
of evidence-based research

00:07:01.221 --> 00:07:05.191
to support the use
of most isolated fiber types.

00:07:05.191 --> 00:07:08.161
Take that supplement Fibersol,
for example.

00:07:08.161 --> 00:07:10.196
Fibersol is
a registered trademark

00:07:10.196 --> 00:07:12.932
of the Matsutani
Chemical Industry Company,

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:14.968
the one who invented it.

00:07:14.968 --> 00:07:17.003
"Looking to increase
the fiber content

00:07:17.003 --> 00:07:18.605
of a finished product?

00:07:18.605 --> 00:07:21.741
Check out
our innovation success stories."

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:25.612
Eat your donut cookie
whipped cream milkshake,

00:07:25.612 --> 00:07:27.580
it’s got fiber!

00:07:28.782 --> 00:07:30.483
Maybe better to stick to foods

00:07:30.483 --> 00:07:34.087
that were invented instead
by Mother Nature.

